Practical 2.5 : Filtering and Maximum Value Extraction

• Create a NumPy array.
• Apply filtering techniques.
• Return maximum values from the array using conditional  filtering.

code :- 

import numpy as np
# Create a NumPy array
arr = np.array([10, 25, 15, 40, 30, 50, 20])
print("Original Array:")
print(arr)
# Filtering values greater than 25
filtered = arr[arr > 25]
print("Values greater than 25:")
print(filtered)
# Find maximum value from the filtered array
max_value = np.max(filtered)
print("Maximum value from filtered array:")
print(max_value)
